{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = {\n 'parent_trial':'g1-r0001-mass_m1_q1',\n 'study':{\n  'id':'g1-value-preservation-query-factorial',\n  'protocol_ref':'1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216',\n  'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w1','g1-r0000-exchange_q0_w1','g1-r0000-exchange_q1_w0','g1-r0000-exchange_q0_w0','g1-r0001-mass_m1_q1','g1-r0001-mass_m0_q1','g1-r0001-mass_m1_q0','g1-r0001-mass_m0_q0'],\n  'question':'Does an uncompressed history-value path improve two-round field/history exchange after count scaling, and does its value depend on refreshed queries? Observations: DIN click AUC=0.655544; original exchange q1/w1=0.647458, q0/w1=0.645457, q1/w0=0.640740, q0/w0=0.632297. Mass m1/q1=0.653330 versus m0/q1=0.640630, and m1/q0=0.651864 versus m0/q0=0.640878. Count scaling helped in both query conditions, but every exchange trial still loses to DIN. For long histories, DIN=0.657803 versus mass m1/q1=0.653757; buy AUC also trails 0.870182 versus 0.857668. These are single-seed observations, not repeated support. All nine executions succeeded; no execution failure is inferred from a predictive loss.',\n  'hypothesis':'The remaining deficit may partly reflect discarding original field/action embedding directions through the event projection and normalization, independently of count scale. Let W2 be the second strict-masked, sqrt(n)-scaled attention matrix, and H the original concatenated history embeddings (six item fields plus action, Dv=112 at embedding_dim=16). Compute s=mean_fields(W2) H. Both treatments expose a learned linear rank-32 reconstruction U D s to otherwise identical towers; the candidate adds the parameter-free identity residual s. This preserves direct value information while keeping field-conditioned retrieval in the evolving low-dimensional exchange state. Query refresh Q is crossed with the value residual R. A positive R effect supports this particular direct value route; a positive R-by-Q interaction is separately needed to support their complementarity. It does not prove a global rank bound on the original field stack or establish a novel mechanism.',\n  'nearest_work':[\n   {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived exact-version primary text, lines 250-277: target-dependent weighted sums of original embeddings and unnormalized weights. We inherit the idea of preserving embedding values, but use mean field-query attention after two exchange rounds, strict masked softmax times sqrt(n), and a raw residual versus learned rank-32 reconstruction. This is not exact DIN reproduction.'},\n   {'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source lines 198-282 uses repeated cross-attention with shared sequence K/V and token-specific query/output matrices. We retain repeated retrieval from our local family, use shared query/output projections and field mixers, and expose original embedding values outside the 32-channel state. No EST heterogeneous FFNs or reproduction claim.'},\n   {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source lines 241-313 aggregates hubs and broadcasts affine signals. Our inherited field-mean affine event writer is fixed in all cells; no task hubs, task routing, or mask-free attention. Its contribution is not re-estimated here.'},\n   {'source_ref':'unirank-benchmark-v2','verification':'read','difference':'Section 2.3 identifies EST/INFNet layer-wise interaction and UniMixer raw-history flattening. We keep event retrieval and add a compact pooled value route rather than flattening all 100 events into a tokenizer. Original EST/INFNet paper detail is unavailable through the registry; novelty relative to those papers remains unverified.'}\n  ],\n  'inherited_components':[\n   'From history_g1_r0001_mass_m1_q1.py, SHA256 8b8174c6d4d9bc10b4a80989cc584ceb3c709c2db9efb4987d51e0410927ccd2: sparse embeddings16, field projections32, two FieldMix blocks, strict-masked readers with sqrt(n) scaling, field-conditioned writer, visible-prefix position scalar, raw current-field skip and log-count scalar, Dice towers128/64.',\n   'Frozen official_offline inputs, all four labels, host scratch training, default sum of four unweighted BCEs, seed20262027, one epoch, batch8192, optimizers, precision and complete validation are unchanged.',\n   'Accepted DIN baseline source hash independently matches candidate.py at entry and read-only baseline_reference.py. Host protocol reports pinned data identity and readiness; raw parquet and host training execution are unavailable in this proposal-only workspace, so those readiness checks are inherited rather than independently repeated.'\n  ],\n  'proposed_difference':'Return existing attention weights from each reader. At the second read, average weights over field queries and pool original masked history embeddings into one 112-dimensional vector. Pass it through bias-free 112->32->112 linear layers in every cell. R=1 adds the original pooled vector to the reconstruction; R=0 exposes only the reconstruction. Append the resulting 112 values to the same tower inputs in all four cells. Q=1 uses first_fields for the second read; Q=0 reuses first_query, exactly as in the prior factorial. The writer remains active in both Q conditions, so Q=0 is a fixed-query control, not absence of all iterative exchange. The raw route reads original embeddings, not rewritten events; only selection weights depend on rewritten events. All four modules instantiate the same parameters in the same order, and all learned modules remain active. Sparse widths and loss are unchanged.',\n  'predictions':[\n   'Primary predeclared contrasts: dR_Q1=AUC(value_r1_q1)-AUC(value_r0_q1) and dR_Q0=AUC(value_r1_q0)-AUC(value_r0_q0). Positive values in both cells would support local value preservation more strongly than a gain only against the old narrower-head ancestor.',\n   'Complementarity contrast I=dR_Q1-dR_Q0 is predicted positive. If I is nonpositive, report no support for value-preservation/query-refresh synergy even if R improves prediction.',\n   'Quality target: value_r1_q1 exceeds the ancestor 0.653330 and preferably DIN 0.655544 in full-population click AUC. All four task AUC/Logloss and cost remain necessary; a click gain with worse auxiliary performance is a tradeoff, not uniform improvement.',\n   'Exploratory localization: inspect the already established empty,1-16,17-64,>64 history bins with sample/positive/negative counts (negative=samples-positives). The ancestor >64 deficit motivates inspection but no unique long-history response is required. Empty histories have s=0 exactly before training; trained models can nevertheless differ there through globally learned weights. Do not invent unavailable frequency/composition diagnostics.',\n   'All four variants have identical learned parameter counts and tower shapes; with Dv112, predicted delta to ancestor is 2*112*32 + 4*112*128 = 64512 dense parameters: total32378628/dense585412/embedding31793216. Confirm host counts. Memory and latency need measurement; equal parameters do not imply equal effective capacity or equal compute.'\n  ],\n  'falsifiers':[\n   'Both matched R effects are nonpositive: no local support for this direct raw-value residual implementation; do not conclude all value-preserving mechanisms are ineffective.',\n   'Only the rank-32 controls improve versus the ancestor: the larger common readout or a new value aggregation path can explain the family gain; the raw identity residual lacks support.',\n   'Interaction I<=0: the proposed complementarity is unsupported, even if the residual has a useful main effect.',\n   'Nonfinite empty-history output, padding-value sensitivity, wrong task output shape or host resource-cap violation invalidates the implementation before predictive interpretation.',\n   'If all cells remain below DIN or cost rises without useful quality, retain DIN as incumbent; a controlled mechanistic contrast within a losing family is not a successful replacement.'\n  ],\n  'alternative_explanations':[\n   'Identity addition changes scale, conditioning, initialization geometry and implicit regularization, as well as bypassing a rank-32 map. This batch identifies the composite residual route, not pure information rank. A scale-matched or fixed full-rank transform replacement would be a discriminating follow-up if it wins.',\n   'The common extra rank-32 reconstruction and wider tower can explain improvement relative to old trials. Use within-batch R contrasts for attribution; old trials are historical anchors only.',\n   'Averaging field-query weights may dilute target-specific evidence; failed raw pooling would not refute per-field raw-value access.',\n   'Existing field states retain multiple query summaries and raw current fields, so compressing each event to32 is not proof of a global32-dimensional information bottleneck.',\n   'One seed, adaptive selection of the question from validation, rare auxiliary positives and repeated user exposures limit uncertainty claims. No user-cluster confidence interval or significance claim is fabricated.'\n  ],\n  'contrasts':[\n   {'parent_ref':'g1-r0001-mass_m1_q1','intervention':'value_r1_q1: refreshed queries and original-value identity residual on top of active rank-32 reconstruction.','control':'value_r0_q1: same refreshed queries and active reconstruction, identity residual removed.','held_fixed':['All parameter shapes, initialization order and tower widths','Input information, frozen host recipe, loss, seed and data passes','Masking, sqrt(n), log-count, writer and original pooled vector computation'],'remaining_confounds':['Residual affects scale and optimization in addition to direct value access.','End-to-end training changes attention weights between arms; this is a trained-route contrast, not fixed-checkpoint mediation.'],'decision_if_supported':'Retain as preliminary support for a direct value route; check DIN/ancestor quality and costs, then plan a scale-controlled replacement and paired repetition.','decision_if_not_supported':'Retain the negative receipt; consider whether aggregation dilution or scale calls for one discriminating follow-up, without declaring a mechanism refutation.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g1-r0001-mass_m1_q0','intervention':'value_r1_q0: original-value residual with fixed second query.','control':'value_r0_q0: rank-32 reconstruction only with fixed second query.','held_fixed':['Same R contrast as Q1','Same learned modules and host recipe across all four cells'],'remaining_confounds':['Q0 still updates event values via the writer.','Single-seed variation.'],'decision_if_supported':'Compare dR_Q0 with dR_Q1 to distinguish a general readout benefit from query-refresh complementarity.','decision_if_not_supported':'If Q1 improves and Q0 does not, treat interaction as preliminary and reserve repetitions; if neither improves, raw residual is unsupported.'},\n   {'parent_ref':'g1-r0001-mass_m1_q1','intervention':'Q refresh in each R stratum and difference-in-differences I=(r1q1-r0q1)-(r1q0-r0q0).','control':'Fixed Q in each R stratum; compare all four cells before selecting. Historical DIN and mass trials anchor performance/cost only.','held_fixed':['Four cells have identical instantiated parameters','Mass scaling and writer enabled','Four-label scoring and click selection'],'remaining_confounds':['Query refresh is only one component of iterative exchange.','No independent seed support or fixed-state counterfactual.','New head width precludes a one-factor comparison to old mass trials.'],'decision_if_supported':'Only a positive I supports complementarity locally. Freeze a later selected suite and closest controls before held-out assessment.','decision_if_not_supported':'Report additive or antagonistic effects as observed. Select by validation click AUC and measured cost; keep DIN if no candidate beats it.'}\n  ],\n  'cost_plan':{\n   'estimate_ref':'baseline-din=328.91s complete; latest mass cells=340.59,341.69,344.01,340.56s complete. Runtime conservative full unit481.35s, per-trial cap1203.37s, remaining167383.74s at context creation; research wall clock hard deadline1794132148.3455288. Additional aggregation is one Bx1x100 by Bx100x112 product plus small linear layers and a wider tower, not full field-by-raw-value expansion. Estimate roughly400-550s/cell pending host measurement; reserve4*600=2400s, worst permitted4*1203.37=4813.48s. No training or torch import executed here.',\n   'all_variants_counted':True,\n   'attribution_reserve':'Execute all four factorial cells (including losing controls) under the shared host recipe; costs include preparation, diagnostics, failures and scoring. Reserve at least6000s for a subsequent scale/replacement contrast and two additional paired seeds of the selected candidate and closest control(s), subject to new runtime and phase authorization. Existing nine single-seed results do not replace the new matched controls.',\n   'assessment_reserve':'Reserve at least6000s for a later frozen assessment suite and host execution/uncertainty work. Current phase has no withheld access. Freeze candidate sources/configurations/checkpoints, closest references/ablations, repetition seeds and assessment commands before requesting held-out assessment. Withheld results stay in the closed archive and cannot guide further search.',\n   'stop_rule':'Do not start any host unit unless current remaining budget covers its conservative cost and reserves; never raise the hard deadline or cap. On resource/finite/masking failure preserve the receipt and re-evaluate feasibility; no automatic duplicate execution when status is unknown. If no useful admissible contrast fits, stop with the best supported existing model. This submission ends at proposal; host owns subsequent checks and training.'\n  }\n },\n 'variants':[],\n 'knowledge_assessments':[]\n}\nfor r,q in [(1,1),(0,1),(1,0),(0,0)]:\n name=f'value_r{r}_q{q}'\n p['variants'].append({'name':name,'file':'candidate.py' if (r,q)==(1,1) else name+'.py','role':'candidate' if (r,q)==(1,1) else 'control','config':{'embedding_dim':16,'token_dim':32,'refresh_query':bool(q),'mass_scaling':True,'raw_value_residual':bool(r)},'note':f'Prospective factorial R={r},Q={q}; no measured outcome. Standalone module; same active learned modules and head sizes as all four cells. Host reproduction: instantiate Model(feature_map, **this config) with the frozen host recipe and default four-task BCE; do not train in coding workspace. Source identity and exact configs are frozen in this proposal for this validation batch only.'})\nnames=[v['name'] for v in p['variants']]\nassessments=[\n ('unirank-method-est','used','Prior executed retrieval family is a useful controlled trajectory but still loses to DIN. Pinned benchmark attention source inspected; original paper text unavailable.','Retain two shared-projection strict-masked retrieval rounds; return final attention weights for value-preserving readout.','No token-specific query/output matrices or feature-specific FFNs. Raw-value residual versus rank-32 reconstruction is the new intervention.','Nonpositive R effects reject local benefit; nonpositive interaction rejects complementarity.',names),\n ('unirank-method-infnet','used','Writer remains inherited and fixed; prior write contrasts do not establish INFNet effectiveness or isolate writer value in this new batch. Pinned benchmark broadcast source inspected.','Keep field-mean-conditioned affine writer active identically in all four cells.','No task-specific hubs/action-mask routing; strict score masks rather than benchmark mask-free attention.','Current gains cannot be attributed to writer changes; a later matched writer removal is needed for that claim.',names),\n ('unirank-method-unimixer','considered','Raw-history exposure addresses a related compression issue, but full flattening would change positional sensitivity and dense capacity together.','No flattening or paired streams; pool original values using existing attention before the new readout.','A compact attention-dependent value route preserves the old exchange stack. Original-method novelty is unverified.','If the compact route fails, a matched flattening or per-field raw-value replacement may remain testable.',[]),\n ('unirank-method-onetrans','considered','Latest knowledge-usage reviewed. No new evidence here justifies adding full joint attention or progressive reduction to this contrast.','None of pyramid reduction or mixed FFNs adopted.','Retain the two-round local exchange lineage; no OneTrans reproduction or efficacy claim.','A later matched full-attention candidate may supersede this family; present trials cannot refute it.',[]),\n ('unirank-method-zenith','rejected','Latest knowledge-usage reviewed. Identifier-capacity changes lack frequency diagnostics and would confound the value-route contrast.','None; sparse widths stay16.','No identifier table expansion.','Future authorized frequency diagnostics could justify reconsidering; no external-method ineffectiveness claim.',[])\n]\nfor kid,decision,rationale,mechanism,difference,falsifier,variants in assessments:\n p['knowledge_assessments'].append({'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':rationale,'transformed_mechanism':mechanism,'variant_names':variants,'nearest_work_difference':difference,'falsifier':falsifier})\nPath('/workspace/proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(p,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote prospective proposal.json: four factorial cells, no experiment executed.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
